Autosaved classification CSVs land here.

This is the default location: `./Classifications`, relative to wherever you
launch the tool from (created automatically if it doesn't exist yet). Pass
`--classifications-dir PATH` to any of the three tools (mosaic, 1-by-1, lobby)
to use a different directory instead.

Mosaic tool:
  no seed:   classification_mosaic_autosave_{name}_{n_stamps}_{ncols}_99.csv
  with seed: classification_mosaic_autosave_{name}_{n_stamps}_{ncols}_{nrows}_{seed}.csv

1-by-1 viewer:
  no seed:   classification_single_{name}_{n_stamps}.csv
  with seed: classification_single_{name}_{n_stamps}_{seed}.csv

When a name is already taken, the file that moves aside says why in its own
name rather than carrying a bare number. Two cases:

  -new_dataset_N   the name was taken by a *different* dataset. Pass -N name
                   to give your sessions distinct names and avoid this.
  -simultaneous_N  another viewer is grading this same session right now. Its
                   file is left untouched and this viewer's grades go here, so
                   neither set is lost; reconcile them afterwards.

Both count up (_1, _2, ...) as the situation repeats. Files named with the
older "-(N)" suffix are still found, read and resumed; that suffix is simply
not written any more, since parentheses have to be quoted or escaped in a
shell before you can copy or move the file.
